{"diagnosis": "Recent results show a clear pattern: simplification wins, added recurrence complexity loses. In retrieval/layered_shallow, cutting visits 3->2 kept exact at 1.0 and was promoted, while matched_damping cost ~0.01 (0.9902 vs 1.0). In repair/tree_region, cycles=2+rlt collapsed to 0.5176 and latent_steps=3+verifier_visits=2+visits=4 collapsed to 0.498 — i.e., extra feedback/latent machinery hurt, not helped. For deduction/kernel_h4 the incumbent is already at the ceiling (dev_exact 1.0, ece ~7e-5, exact_by_visit [1,1,1], adaptive_visits 1.0), so the realistic path to improvement is FLOP/visit reduction with exactness preserved, not accuracy gains. Note the incumbent's adaptive early-stop already halts at visit 1, so visits=3 is partly redundant. Risk: this family is at 1.0, so any change must be judged against a high bar; the 0.005 promotion margin means even small exactness losses get rejected.",
  "proposals": [
    {"config": {"visits": 2}, "rationale": "exact_by_visit is [1.0,1.0,1.0] and adaptive_visits is 1.0, so the third visit contributes no measured exactness; halving/trimming visits should cut per-instance FLOPs by ~1/3 (3346176 -> ~2.23M, since per-visit cost ~1.115M) with exactness unchanged. Action-space dimension is small (<=16 candidates), so two visits suffice for the dominance-kernel reduction.", "predicted_dev_exact": 1.0, "falsification": "dev_exact drops below 0.995 (below the incumbent minus the 0.005 promotion margin), or visits no longer reduce FLOPs as expected."},
    {"config": {"latent_steps": 1}, "rationale": "Latent refinement has no measured benefit here: the answer state reaches exactness in visit 1. Reducing latent_steps 2->1 removes one net(x+y+z) pass per visit, cutting the latent MLP FLOPs by ~1/3 of the recurrence cost (hidden=32, 24+8+1 typed features; ~2*(hidden*(in+hidden)) flops per latent step, on the order of 2e4-4e4 per candidate-set step, so total savings are modest but FLOPs/visit drop ~10-15%). The dominance relation is a sparse, near-deterministic rule, so one latent step should suffice.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.985, "falsification": "dev_exact falls below 0.95 (a regression beyond noise) or ece degrades materially."},
    {"config": {"ldt_projection": true}, "rationale": "The host verifier already returns structured per-candidate diagnostics each visit; ldt_projection clamps certified candidate scores with sound host certificates, which is exactly the failure mode of a dominance kernel (a candidate wrongly kept/eliminated). It adds no parameters (params stay ~11683) and no extra verifier calls (verifier_visits unchanged at 1). Expected to tighten exactness/ece at zero accuracy risk if certificates are sound; worst case it clamps a wrongly-certified candidate and costs ~0.01 like in the repair arm.", "predicted_dev_exact": 0.995, "falsification": "dev_exact drops below 0.99 or verifier_calls/FLOPs increase beyond the incumbent without exactness gain."}
  ]}
